{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like","id":81399,"title":"What will you Pantheons be like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-27T21:00:46-08:00","id":81399,"title":"What will you Pantheons be like?","content":"Even though it may still be a ways off, it looks like we will be getting rules for how Pantheons form this time around (in Demigod 2e I believe). With that being the case, I'm curious as to what sort of Pantheon your Scion groups will form. Is there any unifying concept to your group that might be the basis for a PSP (not sure if the concept of these will make it through to 2e though).<br /> <br /> As for myself... unfortunately, the group I was playing with has gone its seperate ways for the time being (new work scheduels... moves... ect) and the Scion game I was set to start never manifested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Once I can get a new group together and win them over on Scion... we'll see what we come up with (though hopefully the new rules will be out by then).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T21:39:26-08:00","id":81414,"title":"","content":"My Pantheon will be my own construction. My Scion game will be about the players playing themselves. Kind of like Everworld. They find out that eons ago the world was ruled by beings of immense power. There was a schism among them though. Some wanted to rule over humans, these became the Gods as we know them. The others were friends to mankind &amp; so a war was fought. The Titans lost &amp; were thrown down by the Gods. But a peace was made. The world was split &amp; the Gods left to rule over their subjects. &amp; our world that remained turned to technology &amp; only remember the war as myth. The characters will play as the long descendants to those that tried to protect mankind. I have invented an Archetype for each of my players, like a personal god.<br /> <br /> The Artificer<br /> The Stormcrow<br /> The Windrunner<br /> The Moon's Herald<br /> The Bard<br /> The Wyrd<br /> etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","user":"Aermas","date":". 02-28-2014, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:05:54-08:00","id":81575,"title":"","content":"Forming your own pantheon would probably be a startlingly dangerous and difficult prospect for almost any group. So much so that I am curious what kind of mechanical benefits they will include to overcome the nearly overwhelming social backlash from such an action. I am also interested to see what metaphysical steps will be required to undertake such an action, given that it is currently only reasonable possible with the intervention of the Wyrd or Arbiter.<br /> <br /> On the old forums I did a poll to see how many groups ever created their own pantheons, and the result was 5%. I am curious to see how much this number changes once actual rules are in place to facilitate the event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:42:45-08:00","id":81734,"title":"","content":"I think the reasn why so few actually created their own pantheon in 1e was because there were no rules or guidelines to do so. Even if you walked out on your Parent's pantheon and told them to never call you again... you were still stuck as part of that Pantheon. There was no way to actually break the bonds of fate that tied you to them. Additionally, without your own PSP, claiming you were part of a new pantheon was hard to sell to others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:59:46-08:00","id":81743,"title":"","content":"My pantheon was from another world...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T13:39:49-08:00","id":81762,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a character who believes in the <i>first age</i> mankind was defined by nature. Surviving the storm or the next winter shaped humanity, the Titans were the rulers of this age.<br /> <br /> The <i>second age</i> was the age of law. Kings, priests and rules defined humanity. The Gods were the rulers of the second age.<br /> <br /> The <i>third age</i> only just beginning will be the age of technology. Engineers and inventors will create devices who's utility shapes humanity. He wishes to form a Parthenon, all sons of various knowledge or inventor gods, to be the rulers of the third age.<br /> <br /> <br /> Expect transhumanism, super intelligence, AI and utopianism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:41:14-08:00","id":81837,"title":"","content":"Also, I think a reason why there were few pantheons, in a political standpoint, is that any new pantheons might be seen by the original six to be possible threats to their authority as well. Still, I wouldn't be surprised to see a thread for a fan-splat of the Justice League or Avengers as a pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T21:09:09-08:00","id":81923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=81734#post81734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the reasn why so few actually created their own pantheon in 1e was because there were no rules or guidelines to do so. Even if you walked out on your Parent's pantheon and told them to never call you again... you were still stuck as part of that Pantheon. There was no way to actually break the bonds of fate that tied you to them. Additionally, without your own PSP, claiming you were part of a new pantheon was hard to sell to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think it has much less to do with that and a lot more to do with the fact that people play this game to interact with mythology (especially the gods themselves). Creating your own pantheon tends to distance you from that mythology. Many players sit down and pick their divine parent because of the potentially awesome interactions with not only that parent, but also the entire pantheon of that parent. Very few players sit down to make their character with the intention of abandoning their pantheon. Stranger things have been known to happen, though!<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=81837#post81837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think a reason why there were few pantheons, in a political standpoint, is that any new pantheons might be seen by the original six to be possible threats to their authority as well. Still, I wouldn't be surprised to see a thread for a fan-splat of the Justice League or Avengers as a pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>From an IC perspective it would be incredibly difficult to form your own pantheon. Doing so would involve burning bridges, losing safety nets, losing metaphysical power, choosing to disappoint gods with epic charisma, resisting the reasonable arguments of gods with epic manipulation, triggering chain reactions of virtues, potentially angering fate, and generally owing a lot of people a lot of favors.<br /> <br /> <b>And in return, you gain... a different PSP? That's about it.</b><br /> <br /> There a few situations where it might be necessary, though. Such as gathering together the remaining survivors of a Ragnarok level divine extinction event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 03-01-2014, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T21:32:31-08:00","id":81934,"title":"","content":"Okay... I think we're straying from the actual intent... I'm not talking about making up Pantheons like Avengers or Justice League... I'm talking about the pantheons the Players are forming with their characters. Remember, the players are playing characters that will... with luck, become Gods in their own right.<br /> <br /> Many people tend to form bonds with those they associate with that are as strong as any familial bond... in some cases far stronger. Many band of Scions are formed from Scions of multiple pantheons... and most would rather trust their teamates that their own divine parents (and the rest of their families). So why wouldn't they form their own pantheon? Many groups tend to have their members specialized in certain areas, much like other pantheons, right? Of course, the interaction with one's original Pantheon is also a great source of adventure... but sooner or later there will be tension between what they want and what the player/character wants.<br /> <br /> Not all players will want to form their own patheons... some might want to take over and revitalize their current pantheon (especially those bands formed from Scions of a single Pantheon). Even if they don't, sooner or later most players will want to be the one's calling the shots... which isn't easy when there is someone above you who believes they can order you around (name one player who likes being told by an NPC [even a God] what to do and how to do it).<br /> <br /> In the game I was going to run (before outside forces drew my group apart), the final act in the game was going to have my players and their characters (newly rissen to the God Tier) transported about 100 years into the future, to deal with a world tranformed by the final battle of the Titan War. The Old Pantheons were gone, the Titans were dormant (possibly commatose), human civilization was in ruins, and the world was nothing like they remembered. Only the Scions of the Gods survived... some of which have also rissen to Godhood in the aftermath of the war. Now it would be up to my players to rebuild civilization and tame this wild new world... and possibly confront the New Gods that have rissen to fill the vacume left when the Old Pantheons fell. Hopefully one day I will get the chance to run this game (I sill have my notes somewhere).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T22:48:25-08:00","id":81960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=81934#post81934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many people tend to form bonds with those they associate with that are as strong as any familial bond... in some cases far stronger. Many band of Scions are formed from Scions of multiple pantheons... and most would rather trust their teamates that their own divine parents (and the rest of their families). So why wouldn't they form their own pantheon? Many groups tend to have their members specialized in certain areas, much like other pantheons, right? Of course, the interaction with one's original Pantheon is also a great source of adventure... but sooner or later there will be tension between what they want and what the player/character wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not follow that trusting your teammates means that you will attempt to abandon your pantheon. Especially when your pantheon has invested a large number of resources into your continued existence. They probably would not hesitate to take steps to prevent you from leaving the pantheon, unless you have undertaken extensive groundwork and called in extensive favors beforehand. Except under very specific circumstances, you gain almost nothing from forming your own pantheon.<br /> <br /> For the most part, forming your own pantheon seems to be done for OOC reasons (you think it would be cool), instead of IC reasons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T23:56:21-08:00","id":81968,"title":"","content":"I agree with Iry on this. Liking your friends is no excuse for abandoning your family. Your parent Pantheons would go apeshit. Any Pantheon with Duty, Loyalty or Piety would freak out at the idea of one of their own abandoning them, and those with Vengeance will never forgive you for doing it.<br /> <br /> The Theoi would never even entertain the idea that anyone would want to leave their club of awesomeness. The Netjer would consider it an affront to Ma'at and Piety. The Aztecs know of many ways that such a Scion could donate to the war effort. The Shen would probably swamp you in official paperwork for the next couple of millennia. And so on.<br /> <br /> And, perhaps most importantly, Scions are created with one primary purpose: to be soldiers in the war against the Titans. Any God level Scion is expected to be on call to defend his Pantheon. And you're going to go up to Shango and say, I'm abandoning my post? You would be court-martialled and executed on the spot.<br /> <br /> All this is not to say that I don't want rules for players creating their own Pantheons. I do. The Deva-Yazata split shows clearly that it has happened before, and can happen again. But one should both have a good IC reason or it (as opposed to 'let's climb the mountain cuz it's there') and be well aware that they will likely end up dead, or wishing they were, by the end of it.<br /> <br /> Of course, if they can pull it off, they will be the talk of the Overworld for the next few aeons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-01-2014, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T04:33:31-08:00","id":82046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=81960#post81960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part, forming your own pantheon seems to be done for OOC reasons (you think it would be cool), instead of IC reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of our divine parents are fucking dicks, and I'm tired of working for them is an OOC reason.<br /> Not wanting to live in the Shadow of a drunken womanizing idiot, is an OOC reason.<br /> Being disgusted with the ritualized murder of innocent people and wanting no part of it, is an OOC reason.<br /> <br /> I could go through the every fuckin' Pantheon in Scion and come up with an at least plausibly IC reason for a Scion to decide &quot;Yeah nah, fuck these bitches.&quot; The Implication that no ST would let any of these motivations for seceding fly is frankly insulting.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if the Gods' have a problem, well <i>so what</i>? By this point you are gods too. The Shen wants to send us Paperwork, then we will thank them for all the <i>kindling</i>. Shango wants to kill us, he's welcome to <i>try.</i> And if the Aztecs want blood, <i>they will get it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 03-02-2014, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T05:18:25-08:00","id":82057,"title":"","content":"Hm. Some relevant quotes from Neall:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Current plan for Demigod is to have mechanics on how pantheons are formed or re-formed (''interpretatio romana''). Kind of stands to reason that PCs could take advantage of those. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pantheons are comprised of gods and demigods (and culture heroes who exist on the hero level, but they don't do much, metaphysically speaking). When I mentioned them forming, I didn't mean to imply you, Jane Hero Smith, weren't part of a pantheon on the Hero level - you are. Demigod addresses how pantheons form as social as magical constructs within Fate, but you benefit from those constructs at every level, Origin included. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interpretatio is going to be a thing in 2e. It's something all of the writers are keenly aware of, so we're taking that into account while designing the cosmology. As for PSPs, well. Those have changed a lot already. It's not fair or accurate to describe pantheon membership as a social club with fringe metaphysical benefits...but I wouldn't say it's fair to describe them as permanent mystical bloodlines anymore, either. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a plan for the new edition to more on religion as well as myth. I mean, people believed - and continue to believe! - this stuff. Blood was shed for it. The least we can do is acknowledge the difference between Jupiter Optimus Maximus and the King of Olympus (even if they both wield the three thunderbolts of Tinia, because they're the same dude). When I mentioned interpretatio, I meant it in the more general sense: how other cultures (and pantheons!) look at and interpret gods has an impact, if you consider that the mythology is partially driven by the acts of Gods and Fate. We're also talking about immortal, divine beings who exist over a continuum of thousands of years. People wear a lot of hats in their mayfly lives; how many more so do the gods wear, then? </div> </div> </div>Note that first quote, alluding to how the Theoi were reinterpreted in Rome. That is, becoming the Roman pantheon apparently involved some re-formation of the pantheon on some level.<br /> <br /> Iry's argument appears to be based on the idea that you can't form a new pantheon without leaving your old one. I suspect that's not the case - that you _can_ form another pantheon without leaving your original. After all, it wouldn't be unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T05:45:34-08:00","id":82065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82057#post82057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that first quote, alluding to how the Theoi were reinterpreted in Rome. That is, becoming the Roman pantheon apparently involved some re-formation of the pantheon on some level.<br /> <br /> Iry's argument appears to be based on the idea that you can't form a new pantheon without leaving your old one. I suspect that's not the case - that you _can_ form another pantheon without leaving your original. After all, it wouldn't be unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now THAT I would love to see. It would be cool to see the PC Band evolve into a cross-cultural team of Gods worshipped as a group while still retaining ties to their old Pantheons. Something akin to The Seven Gods of Fortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T07:45:16-08:00","id":82104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82046#post82046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of our divine parents are fucking dicks, and I'm tired of working for them is an OOC reason.<br /> Not wanting to live in the Shadow of a drunken womanizing idiot, is an OOC reason.<br /> Being disgusted with the ritualized murder of innocent people and wanting no part of it, is an OOC reason.<br /> <br /> I could go through the every fuckin' Pantheon in Scion and come up with an at least plausibly IC reason for a Scion to decide &quot;Yeah nah, fuck these bitches.&quot; The Implication that no ST would let any of these motivations for seceding fly is frankly insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abandoning your pantheon does not mean your divine parents will stop trying to make you work for them. If they were fucking dicks, they might be even more inclined to boss you around now that you have so many more enemies and less oversight into how they treat you. Not wanting to live in the shadow of a drunken womanizing idiot has nothing to do with your pantheon status. Leaving your pantheon won't make gods stop expecting you to engage in ritualized murder of innocent people, and may just entice them to try and kill you.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. Those are valid IC complaints for a character to have about their pantheon. It is also entirely possible for a character to be under the impression that trying to abandon his pantheon would result in escaping from the political bullshit of his pantheon. But they will probably discover that it does no such thing, and the intelligent scions in the group are going to realize it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82057#post82057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iry's argument appears to be based on the idea that you can't form a new pantheon without leaving your old one. I suspect that's not the case - that you _can_ form another pantheon without leaving your original. After all, it wouldn't be unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see rules for pantheon reformation and / or sub-pantheons in the new edition. I also definitely agree with Samudra that rules for forming new pantheons should exist. It is just hard as balls to accomplish at the moment, but that may change in the future!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 03-01-2014, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T11:20:02-08:00","id":82175,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=81762#post81762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of a character who believes in the <i>first age</i> mankind was defined by nature. Surviving the storm or the next winter shaped humanity, the Titans were the rulers of this age.<br /> <br /> The <i>second age</i> was the age of law. Kings, priests and rules defined humanity. The Gods were the rulers of the second age.<br /> <br /> The <i>third age</i> only just beginning will be the age of technology. Engineers and inventors will create devices who's utility shapes humanity. He wishes to form a Parthenon, all sons of various knowledge or inventor gods, to be the rulers of the third age.<br /> <br /> <br /> Expect transhumanism, super intelligence, AI and utopianism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This presupposes that progress is always positive. And I don't believe that your expectations are. One man's Heaven is another man's Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T15:04:59-08:00","id":82338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82104#post82104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong. Those are valid IC complaints for a character to have about their pantheon. It is also entirely possible for a character to be under the impression that trying to abandon his pantheon would result in escaping from the political bullshit of his pantheon. But they will probably discover that it does no such thing, and the intelligent scions in the group are going to realize it.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Post edited by moderator. Darksider.</span> You're so convinced of your own <i>helplessness</i>, of your own <i>powerlessness </i>in a game where you play a <i>God. </i><br /> <br /> Where you're a larger than life hero, oh but, never defy your parents. Never mind the Theoi's origins, their oldest myth began with them doing that very thing. If a drunken asshat who cannot keep his dick in his pants and the family that spends most of their legends infighting can do it and succeed, then why not me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":".  Personal insult/attack. 03-02-2014, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T15:44:00-08:00","id":82375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82175#post82175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This presupposes that progress is always positive. And I don't believe that your expectations are. One man's Heaven is another man's Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course progress is always positive. I'm going to be in charge of it!<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. <a href=\"http://www.gapminder.org/world\" target=\"_blank\">Check out the stats</a>, progress has been pretty sweet in the last few decades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,