was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T23:48:16-08:00","id":82531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82383#post82383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not aware of any man's Hell involving nobody dying of Dysentery. Or the crippled being able to walk again. Or the blind to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it might involve income inequality becoming capability inequality as the rich are able to afford cybernetics that the poor cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T00:35:37-08:00","id":82541,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please keep the conversation civil, no need to insult other people if you disagree with them.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T00:36:57-08:00","id":82542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82531#post82531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it might involve income inequality becoming capability inequality as the rich are able to afford cybernetics that the poor cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm ok with that. If the poor a living Bill Gates like lives of wealth and luxury, who cares what the rich are doing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T03:16:46-08:00","id":82573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82338#post82338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're so convinced of your own <i>helplessness</i>, of your own <i>powerlessness </i>in a game where you play a <i>God. </i><br /> <br /> Where you're a larger than life hero, oh but, never defy your parents. Never mind the Theoi's origins, their oldest myth began with them doing that very thing. If a drunken asshat who cannot keep his dick in his pants and the family that spends most of their legends infighting can do it and succeed, then why not me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are arguing two different issues which probably should not be conflated. The first issue is whether or not escaping from your pantheon should be possible. The second issue is whether or not forming your own pantheon with your friends is a positive thing.<br /> <br /> Regarding the first issue, you have the ability to theoretically do anything as a player character. If you set your mind towards removing yourself from your pantheon, then your storyteller is probably going to make that goal something you can accomplish. But not without challenge. Not without difficulty. Not without hardships. Not without sacrifices. Most of the greatest accomplishments in Scion should probably be stories of their own and include rising actions, climax, falling actions, and finally a resolution. Yes, forming your own pantheon should absolutely be possible for a wide variety of reasons. You could literally base entire campaigns around the concept:<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b> A post Ragnarok level divine extinction event requires you to unite the arguing and disparate gods beneath a single banner because you have an ancient relic that affords supernatural protection to anyone who swears allegiance beneath it.<br /> <br /> <b>2)</b> Two greater titans are crashing against a pantheon and slowly wearing them down, so the gods hatch a desperate conspiracy to take some of their own children and the children of a few other pantheons and elevate them into their own pantheon. Once the children have ascended to their own pantheon, one of the two greater titans moves away to crush this 'weaker' pantheon. The first pantheon regrets the sacrifice, but collectively rally themselves and finally mount an offensive against the remaining greater titan.<br /> <br /> <b>3)</b> You are a 'criminal' who is languishing in an underworld suffering eternal torment, but you manage a desperate escape. In your harrowing journey you navigate the underworld and release other people similarly being tortured for petty slights. You gather together and overcome all odds, eventually forming your own pantheon to take vengeance upon those who wrong you!<br /> <br /> Regarding the second issue, you have all the difficulties of a single person trying to leave their pantheon multiplied by every other person who is also trying to leave their pantheon to form your own. There are currently no mechanical benefits to forming your own pantheon. Unless your storyteller specifically creates a mechanical benefit, or is specifically running a storyline where creating your own pantheon is the focus, then your mental scions are going to realize it doesn't accomplish anything positive. They are going to make empathy and politics rolls, pop a few mystery or prophecy uses, and discover that a lot of people would be very angry, a lot of other people would try to stop you, a lot more people are going to manipulate you, and a lot of titans would be happy to take advantage of your sudden lack of protection.<br /> <br /> <b>There are so many reasons not to do it, and so many ways the gods could stop you from doing it, that you are probably only going to succeed BECAUSE you are player characters.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 03-02-2014, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T03:29:24-08:00","id":82575,"title":"","content":"To be honest, this thread has devolved away from what I was asking. It has become a discussion on how easy it is to form one's own pantheon... which wasn't the intent of it. I asked simply &quot;What sort or Pantheon would the Scions (players) in your game would create?&quot; The question implies that there was some reason for them to do so (so that argument is moot) and it also implies that they were able to do so (so how easy it is to do so is also a moot point). If it is possible, can we get back to the original intent to see the diversity of Pantheons this community could produce if their Scions were to form their own Pantheons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T03:37:34-08:00","id":82578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82575#post82575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, this thread has devolved away from what I was asking. It has become a discussion on how easy it is to form one's own pantheon... which wasn't the intent of it. I asked simply &quot;What sort or Pantheon would the Scions (players) in your game would create?&quot; The question implies that there was some reason for them to do so (so that argument is moot) and it also implies that they were able to do so (so how easy it is to do so is also a moot point). If it is possible, can we get back to the original intent to see the diversity of Pantheons this community could produce if their Scions were to form their own Pantheons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of it depends on the circumstances and which gods are available to pick from. I would really love to see a pantheon of Aphrodite, Ishtar, Freya, Stribog, Oshun, Tezcatlipoca, and the Morrigan. They could get up to so much trouble.<br /> <br /> This topic is a lot like fantasy football I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T18:51:59-08:00","id":82885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82575#post82575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, this thread has devolved away from what I was asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>This happens a <i>lot</i> in White Wolf (or should I say Onyx Path) forums. This is basically the same thing that would happen if you asked what would go down if the Masquerade was broken in the Vampire forums. Though to a different degree, as utterly defeatist as Iry is being about this, she's not claiming it's <i>absolutely impossible.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is possible, can we get back to the original intent to see the diversity of Pantheons this community could produce if their Scions were to form their own Pantheons? </div> </div> </div>A Pantheon that was made entirely from Scions would be an interesting melting pot, assuming it was made up for Scions from a mixed group. Aztec Warriors standing side by side Viking Skalds. That sort of thing.<br /> For some reason I see it being made of more Modern Concepts, Gods of Millitary Conflict, of Flight and Space Travel. Virtues would probably be the hardest thing to nail down, because that's what happens when such disperate cultures come together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T19:09:02-08:00","id":82897,"title":"","content":"Hmm...modern concepts...<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of Guy Murchie's Seven Mysteries of Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T05:42:07-08:00","id":83110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82885#post82885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though to a different degree, as utterly defeatist as Iry is being about this, she's not claiming it's <i>absolutely impossible.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I've repeatedly claimed that it is entirely possible! Just extremely difficult and generally a bad idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=82575#post82575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is possible, can we get back to the original intent to see the diversity of Pantheons this community could produce if their Scions were to form their own Pantheons?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a rather hard question, because it usually boils down to &quot;whoever is currently in our band, plus a few others&quot;. Are you just asking people to tell you about the characters in their group, except what they would be like if they were gods in the same pantheon?<br /> <br /> <i>For example, John has Epic Charisma, Epic Wits, Artistry and Justice. He hopes to become a god of game design. Anne has Epic Manipulation, Epic Intelligence, Artistry and Mystery. She hopes to become a goddess of writing and occult lore. Iry has Epic Charisma, Epic Intelligence, Mystery and Prophecy. He hopes to become a god of game design. Telgar has Epic Stamina, Epic Intelligence, Guardian and Justice. He hopes to become a god of photographers. Watcher has Epic Stamina, Epic Charisma, Guardian and Mystery. He hopes to become a god of historic knowledge. Aynie has Epic Charisma, Epic Manipulation, Artistry and Moon. She is not sure what she wants to become a goddess of.<br /> <br /> As a pantheon they have divided into three groups. Anne creates a vast amount of content for her worshipers and has built up a cult. John makes sure the cult is built upon decent mechanics and visits justice upon those who disagree. Iry creates content for his own worshipers, but has a smaller cult and often disagrees with John. Telgar is the keeper of useful lists, but his lower socials cause conflict even though he means well. Watcher is always happy to help his followers, but sacrifices too much of himself. Aynie serves as the bridge between them all, though she is as changing as the moon she represents. Together they fight crime.</i><br /> <br /> Something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:41:13-08:00","id":83139,"title":"","content":"I think that certain modern ideas that deities might embody could be problematic unless the focus is on older gods evolving into them. A god of the internet or AI would find it near impossible to contend with a god of the sun who decided a magnetic storm on an epic scale would make a nice display, or a storm god that got on his/her high horse and revealed what a godly lightning bolt can do when s/he chooses to ignores physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T07:43:49-08:00","id":83162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83139#post83139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that certain modern ideas that deities might embody could be problematic unless the focus is on older gods evolving into them. A god of the internet or AI would find it near impossible to contend with a god of the sun who decided a magnetic storm on an epic scale would make a nice display, or a storm god that got on his/her high horse and revealed what a godly lightning bolt can do when s/he chooses to ignores physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they find that problematic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:17:10-08:00","id":83180,"title":"","content":"Unless it's an older deity that has the basics already understood a new god can't compete. A robot god going against the full power of nature isn't going to end well for the robot. A deity that can ignore physics versus a deity whose function relies on physics. A living lightning bolt that can dismiss &quot;ground&quot; is frightening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:42:20-08:00","id":83207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83180#post83180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it's an older deity that has the basics already understood a new god can't compete. A robot god going against the full power of nature isn't going to end well for the robot. A deity that can ignore physics versus a deity whose function relies on physics. A living lightning bolt that can dismiss &quot;ground&quot; is frightening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think a robot god is restricted to physics any more or less than any other god. When it comes time for a lightning bolt to deal damage to a robot created by a robot god, the lightning bolt doesn't get any bonus dice. Isn't following the laws of physics just a personal choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T11:54:26-08:00","id":83337,"title":"","content":"If that's the case then it's not exactly a robot then. From my point of view, the deities that master the basic building blocks of the universe, wrested from ancient deities, create and impose the functions, constants, and laws of reality. This should take time. Eons. New deities would be formed under this superstructure. So...their already handicapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T13:27:38-08:00","id":83418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83337#post83337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case then it's not exactly a robot then. From my point of view, the deities that master the basic building blocks of the universe, wrested from ancient deities, create and impose the functions, constants, and laws of reality. This should take time. Eons. New deities would be formed under this superstructure. So...their already handicapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of modern science is totally awesome, but a few centuries ago Alchemy would have been modern science. A few centuries from now, a modern god of the internet is probably going to look just as ignorant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T13:50:44-08:00","id":83438,"title":"","content":"Old deities don't need modern science. *shrugs* From your posts, I'm guessing you'd prefer the older deities to be seen as unnecessary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:29:32-08:00","id":83470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83438#post83438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old deities don't need modern science. *shrugs* From your posts, I'm guessing you'd prefer the older deities to be seen as unnecessary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some gods are thousands of years old. Some are only a few hundred years old. What seems like modern science to us now is going to look antiquated and mistaken in the future. I think a god can build a robot according to today's standards, or the standards of a century ago, and still get equal effectiveness. Only the fluff changes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:40:34-08:00","id":83476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83139#post83139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that certain modern ideas that deities might embody could be problematic unless the focus is on older gods evolving into them. A god of the internet or AI would find it near impossible to contend with a god of the sun who decided a magnetic storm on an epic scale would make a nice display, or a storm god that got on his/her high horse and revealed what a godly lightning bolt can do when s/he chooses to ignores physics.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's like saying a god of farming can't beat a god of war in a fight.<br /> <br /> 1) It's true.<br /> 2) Who cares?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T15:50:13-08:00","id":83550,"title":"","content":"Your game. Your rules. Are scions created spontaneously, or were they scions of another older deity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T15:58:12-08:00","id":83556,"title":"","content":"Your game. Your rules. Are scions created spontaneously, or were they scions of another older deity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T17:44:14-08:00","id":83635,"title":"","content":"Most groups form for a reason that goes beyond any initial reason for forming. Yes, they may be intitialy formed because the Scions' Divine Parents' brought them together for a specific purpose... but then why did they choose to stay together as a group after that initial purpose was finished? As has been stated before, many groups have no familial ties to each other, so it isn't like they are serving their Pantheons by staying together, right?<br /> <br /> For example, going over the various Scions I've played in the half dozen games I've been in since 1e came out, there seems to be a common theme to them, even though they come from a lot of different Pantheons... that of a primal nature, from an Aesir Wolf Goddess (originally a Scion of Freya), to a God of Creation and Destruction (a Scion of Heaphestus), and even a Goddess of Cycles (life, death and rebirth; originally a Scion of the Morrigan). I have created a Goddess of the Day (a Scion of Amaterasu) and a God of the Night (a Scion of Tezcatlipoca). As a group, they have found common ground in their dedication to the Virtues of Courage, Expression, Intellect and even Endurance; even though not all of them share all of these virtues. Together they have come to represent cycles in the natural world (Predator and Prey, Day and Night, Creation and Destruction and such) and work to preserve those natural cycles in a balance... day gives way to night and then to day again... seasons change but always return in time... that which rises may fall and may then rise again. Nothing is forever except the cycle they have come to represent. That is the Pantheon the Scions I have created would form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:34:06-08:00","id":83683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83110#post83110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IAynie has Epic Charisma, Epic Manipulation, Artistry and Moon. She is not sure what she wants to become a goddess of.[/I]<br /> <br /> Something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm offended that I don't have Health or know what I'm going to be a Goddess of. OFFENDED. Pretty sure I'd be the Goddess of Maniacal Plots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:31:15-08:00","id":83723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83110#post83110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've repeatedly claimed that it is entirely possible! Just extremely difficult and generally a bad idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />This is a rather hard question, because it usually boils down to &quot;whoever is currently in our band, plus a few others&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>At a maximum it could include every Scion to achieve godhood.<br /> <br /> Sure, it's unlikely to get quite that many people, but I feel it'd fill up pretty nicely.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that certain modern ideas that deities might embody could be problematic unless the focus is on older gods evolving into them. </div> </div> </div>Heaven deliver me from Storyteller's nonsense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A god of the internet or AI would find it near impossible to contend with a god of the sun who decided a magnetic storm on an epic scale would make a nice display, or a storm god that got on his/her high horse and revealed what a godly lightning bolt can do when s/he chooses to ignores physics. </div> </div> </div>Only if you insist that only old gods are capable of breaking the laws of Physics.<br /> Given the Scion's get their power from their relation to said gods, we can discard this notion out of hand.<br /> <br /> Also, Zeus could kick the shit out of Dionysus. Yet does that stop Dionysus from gaining worship in his own rite? No? And it can't apply to the Scion's pantheon becauuuuse?<br /> Anyone? Anyone? Bueller?<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah. Can we drop some of the tiresome double standards in this discussion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 03-05-2014, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T21:28:41-08:00","id":83751,"title":"","content":"I don't get it...Hephaesthus <b>has</b> robots. Zeus throws around thunderbolts. They get along fine (or as fine as any of the Theoi get along). More importantly, almost nothing Scions do is mundane. Even if they weren't using Artistry (or some other Forge type Purview) in it's creation, they're designing it with Epic Intelligence. That robot will be light years ahead of any mortal creation, and even mortal creations can stand up to fluctuations in electric current. A divine robot should be able to stand up to a thunderbolt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's like saying a god of farming can't beat a god of war in a fight.<br /> <br /> 1) It's true.<br /> 2) Who cares? </div> </div> </div>Don't discount farming Gods. Demeter brought the World to its knees after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T06:47:18-08:00","id":83924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83723#post83723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you insist that old gods are capable of breaking the laws of Physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e God is clear. This isn't &quot;Sci-ence&quot; it's Sci-on. If you want that changed then there wouldn't be any such thing as gods to begin with and no reason for a game to exist. (Or do you think lifting 50k tons and throwing it lies comfortably within the laws of physics? Especially since any singular being would sink to the ground even if that were possible. Although I think that image is hysterically funny) However, if that's how you prefer your game...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83723#post83723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the Scion's get their power from their relation to said gods, we can discard this notion out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <b>your</b> game.<br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> I've found the exercise of forming pantheons from &quot;titans&quot; pretty cool. The titans would be an older generation of gods that were demonized by the conquering gods and would be trying to find their way back to strength.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T08:58:54-08:00","id":83986,"title":"","content":"'scuse me, Left an only out there. What I meant to say that &quot;only if you insist that <i>only</i> old gods can break the laws of physics.&quot; Funny how one word can change the entire meaning of an entire sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:14:08-08:00","id":84030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83751#post83751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't discount farming Gods. Demeter brought the World to its knees after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't discount science gods either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T11:29:18-08:00","id":84732,"title":"","content":"The idea of a God of Science is a weird. I mean I occasionally invoke Carl Sagan in some threads, but mostly as a joke. Science isn't like the Sea or the Sky, it's a method of processing information and learning. What powers would one give to a God of that? Can he make the Neurons in your brain fire in a spectacularly bizarre way? Turn your blood into hydrochloric acid? Properly explain how to roll THAC0?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 03-05-2014, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T11:48:31-08:00","id":84752,"title":"","content":"What powers do you give Thoth, the god of knowledge, wisdom and writing? (ok, I know he's a couple of other things as well)<br /> <br /> Lets say it was Carl Sagan and ask what he'd have under the current purviews, Epic Intelligence obviously, he was great as a presenter so Epic Charisma, maybe Epic Perception. Next he's an astronomer so he'd obviously get Stars. As a writer and television producer you could justify Artistry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, gods of science work like ye olde gods of knowledge. With perhaps a lot less talk of secrecy and a lot more teaching, and other powers based around what they're famous for discovering or inventing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:47:49-08:00","id":85369,"title":"","content":"Mithra has just a valid claim on being in the Roman pantheon as he does in the Persian/Zoroastrian one. Guanyin would likely be accepted by both Japan and China. Just saying: membership in one pantheon doesn't necessarily preclude membership in another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:34:14-08:00","id":86323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=83139#post83139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that certain modern ideas that deities might embody could be problematic unless the focus is on older gods evolving into them. A god of the internet or AI would find it near impossible to contend with a god of the sun who decided a magnetic storm on an epic scale would make a nice display, or a storm god that got on his/her high horse and revealed what a godly lightning bolt can do when s/he chooses to ignores physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>How, exactly, is that any different from spats and rivalries between classical deities? Do fire gods just shrug and say &quot;yeah whatever&quot; if they raise the ire of a water god, or if the patron or guardian deity of a city-state which rests at the foot of a volcano (like that <b>ever</b> happened in the classical world, amirite?) managed to slight an earth or fire god? All you're really pointing out here is that, indeed, deities of modern and contemporary concepts can indeed have rivalries.<br /> <br /> You're also assuming such gods have <b>no</b> capacity whatsoever to fight back by dint of their own purviews and associations, especially in ways that slip entirely under more antiquated gods' radars. What would Thor <i>really</i> be able to do about Bob, Scion of Loki turned God of Cable TV News, slipping a subliminal message into live global broadcasts that Thor <i>loves</i> blowing donkeys. It probably wouldn't even be until Thor's in avatar form on-stage in TJ until he realizes, &quot;wait a minute, what the hell am I doing...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, worst-case scenario, see Akhenaten and its near-total neutering in the face of monotheism and science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-07-2014, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T16:51:08-08:00","id":86370,"title":"","content":"You're forgetting the reality of physical in-yo-face brutality. If Thor had reason enough he could simply kill Bob. I know that some people fantasize that a nerd in a straight up dirty fight in a back alley is going to go the nerd's way, but if people want a better reflection of reality, the nerd typically gets crushed. Now if one wants to talk how a particular game would go...then that would indeed be a bit different as a storyteller could make that nerd take off the glasses and we can see that he was really Clark Kent all along. Kind of like how a doctor suddenly becomes a god of thunder. But a god of Cable TV versus a God that typically eats Titans for breakfast? That would be some storytelling going around to make that believable. How often does Social beat Physical? <i>NOT THE FACE NOT THE FACE!!!!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T17:29:16-08:00","id":86380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86370#post86370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're forgetting the reality of physical in-yo-face brutality. If Thor had reason enough [...] <b>How often does Social beat Physical</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask Loki. He's the biggest pussy of all the Legend 12 gods that have stats to begin with (I think even Hera could be his ass in a straight-up fight), let alone the biggest pussy of his own pantheon and they have cause enough to smear him from one end of Asgard to the other...why they just don't can't be handwaved with Fate (in fact, there's an entire sidebar in Ragnarok about this). Thor has the biggest beef with Loki this side of Heimdall of the entire pantheon, yet he <i>doesn't</i>.<br /> <br /> Because Thor is a moron, and Loki exploits this to his advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-07-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T18:17:27-08:00","id":86400,"title":"","content":"Loki who got chained up by the Aesir and tortured? Bound on top of three stones with the entrails of his son Narfi until Ragnarok. Which he then gets in that most awkward of moments for those with less then formidable physical talents and gets in a one-on-one fight with Heimdall and subsequently gets killed. (Heimdall bites it as well, but there goes fate.) But I'm sure that Storytellers play out the game differently than the actual literature. After all this is a game. Not reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T21:14:08-08:00","id":86467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86400#post86400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loki who got chained up by the Aesir and tortured? Bound on top of three stones with the entrails of his son Narfi until Ragnarok. Which he then gets in that most awkward of moments for those with less then formidable physical talents and gets in a one-on-one fight with Heimdall and subsequently gets killed. (Heimdall bites it as well, but there goes fate.) But I'm sure that Storytellers play out the game differently than the actual literature. After all this is a game. Not reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the <b>entire</b> Aesir united including Odin, for pulling something so stupid not even he could talk his way out of. And, nice time to pull the Fate card (when it suits you).<br /> <br /> Either way, this entire conversation is tangential. Physical -- even in scion -- does not rule over all, all the time and in every circumstance. Like it or not, this <i>is</i> one of those circumstances in which gods that embrace modernity or start getting tech-savvy could wield a <b>ton</b> of power by harnessing and exploiting mass communications or Zeitgeist to their own ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T21:38:45-08:00","id":86480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86370#post86370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often does Social beat Physical? <i>NOT THE FACE NOT THE FACE!!!!</i></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Most of the time.</b> Social has the greatest power to change the outcome of the story, to turn all of the resources of the enemy into your own resources, to lock down dozens of opponents in combat, and countless other advantages. It is certainly true that a social character only has to screw up once for a physical character to splatter him across the sidewalk, but a clever social character is going to make sure he succeeds for a very long time before that ever happens.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all a moot issue because most characters should have a variety of attributes anyway.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86400#post86400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loki who got chained up by the Aesir and tortured? Bound on top of three stones with the entrails of his son Narfi until Ragnarok. Which he then gets in that most awkward of moments for those with less then formidable physical talents and gets in a one-on-one fight with Heimdall and subsequently gets killed. (Heimdall bites it as well, but there goes fate.) But I'm sure that Storytellers play out the game differently than the actual literature. After all this is a game. Not reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>In many games, that has not happened yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T00:41:31-08:00","id":86569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86400#post86400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loki who got chained up by the Aesir and tortured? Bound on top of three stones with the entrails of his son Narfi until Ragnarok. Which he then gets in that most awkward of moments for those with less then formidable physical talents and gets in a one-on-one fight with Heimdall and subsequently gets killed. (Heimdall bites it as well, but there goes fate.) But I'm sure that Storytellers play out the game differently than the actual literature. After all this is a game. Not reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are ignoring the actual point of Theodrim's argument...that Thor despite all his physical might, can never touch Loki. What you describe has nothing to do with Thor, it is a consequence of him causing the death of <i>Odin's</i> son. Odin, who is himself a Social juggernaut, not Thor, is the one who finally passes sentence on Loki. Thor might relish his chance at revenge, but it was only allowed by the graces of a Social character.<br /> <br /> How often does Social beat Physical, you ask?<br /> <br /> What about Ra, who despite being a frail old man still holds the reins on physical juggernauts like Set and Sekhmet? Who has a whole barge full of physical badasses ready to die for him? And who is Ra ultimately trumped by? Isis, another Goddess of Social might, not Physical.<br /> <br /> When Shiva was rampaging in pain because of the residual energy in Brahma's fifth head, and nobody could hold him down, who stopped him? Sarasvati, with her Epic Charisma and Appearance. This is the same Sarasvati who tricked the demon Kumbhakarna into asking for the gift of eternal sleep when he was going to ask for the throne of the Gods. When Shiva is tricked into giving the power to destroy anything to the demon Bhasmasur and is in danger of being killed himself, who saves him? Mohini, the enchantress Avatara of Vishnu who tricks Bhasmasur into using the power on himself.<br /> <br /> The Mayan Hero Twins win against the Lords of Death by convincing them to allow themselves to be cut to pieces, no questions asked.<br /> <br /> The Dagda is kicked out of his own realm by the trickery of his son Aengus, who receives it for Day and Night.<br /> <br /> Shango, one of the biggest baddest of physical badasses, once boasted that he could defeat any God. When the trickster Eshu asked if that included him, Shango, the great and mighty, was so terrified at what Eshu might do to him that he immediately clarified that he meant all other Gods except Eshu. This is the same Eshu who used his Epic Manipulation to shame the supreme creator of Yoruba mythology, Oludomare, into leaving his own creation behind forever.<br /> <br /> And that's not even counting the one time Hera beat Artemis to a pulp.<br /> <br /> \u200bOverall, in a straight up fight, Physical will beat Social no contest. It's just laughably easy for Social characters to ensure that never happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-08-2014, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T01:14:01-08:00","id":86585,"title":"","content":"<b>Words cannot begin to describe how much win was wrapped into that post, sir.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:26:48-08:00","id":86892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=81934#post81934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... I think we're straying from the actual intent... I'm not talking about making up Pantheons like Avengers or Justice League... I'm talking about the pantheons the Players are forming with their characters. Remember, the players are playing characters that will... with luck, become Gods in their own right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And why not making Pantheons based on your fandom? Just because the Scions became Gods, it doesn't always mean that they'll fall under the same category as their parents. Hell, making a real life would be any comic nerd's wet dream. Knowing that they can back up the claim is an added incentive. Just like that fans of horror movies would make one based on the Universal Monsters line or like that Nursery Rhyne/Fable pantheon that I discussed in another line. Sure there'll be gods and goddesses who represent the modern aspects of modern existence like the Internet and Memes, but don't just dismiss the fact that there will be some Fandom influencing the Band's decision when creating a new pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:41:48-08:00","id":86902,"title":"","content":"This whole social vs physical argument has gotten me thinking: how do epic socials work on people without the appropriate method of perception. I'm thinking things along the lines of Odysseus' men plugging their ears to row past the (presumably possessed of epic socials) Sirens. It also means that in-the-know adversaries could easily get deaf security people in order to mitigate the damage that epic social characters can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:00:05-08:00","id":86914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86569#post86569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are ignoring the actual point of Theodrim's argument...that Thor despite all his physical might, can never touch Loki. What you describe has nothing to do with Thor, it is a consequence of him causing the death of <i>Odin's</i> son. Odin, who is himself a Social juggernaut, not Thor, is the one who finally passes sentence on Loki. Thor might relish his chance at revenge, but it was only allowed by the graces of a Social character.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Heimdall touched him more then enough times to kill him. I guess he forgot to somehow ensure that never happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86569#post86569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often does Social beat Physical, you ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll find far more examples in literature that it doesn't. Because <i>strength</i> (power) is the primary virtue. If one desires a game where it isn't, then that is up to those playing. But don't imagine that reality is the same. It never has been and it never will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:14:49-08:00","id":86924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86902#post86902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole social vs physical argument has gotten me thinking: how do epic socials work on people without the appropriate method of perception. I'm thinking things along the lines of Odysseus' men plugging their ears to row past the (presumably possessed of epic socials) Sirens. It also means that in-the-know adversaries could easily get deaf security people in order to mitigate the damage that epic social characters can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the mythology. In the Mahabharata the blind king Dhritarashtra is still able to see Krishna when he turns his Epic Appearance on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:41:37-08:00","id":86943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86924#post86924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the mythology. In the Mahabharata the blind king Dhritarashtra is still able to see Krishna when he turns his Epic Appearance on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really interesting, but not super-helpful from a game mechanics standpoint. Most rules need to be applied as universally as possible, for simplicity and clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:41:57-08:00","id":86944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86914#post86914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll find far more examples in literature that it doesn't. Because <i>strength</i> (power) is the primary virtue. If one desires a game where it isn't, then that is up to those playing. But don't imagine that reality is the same. It never has been and it never will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, back this claim up with examples, at lest more than Samudra provided.<br /> <br /> Oh, and while you're at it. Only choose examples from mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:24:57-08:00","id":86966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86914#post86914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Heimdall touched him more then enough times to kill him. I guess he forgot to somehow ensure that never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heimdall is at war, under the commands of his Jarl, Odin. This is not a matter of Heimdall's resistance vs. Loki's Manipulation, it's a matter of Odin's Manipulation vs. Loki's Manipulation, and Odin wins out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86914#post86914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll find far more examples in literature that it doesn't. Because <i>strength</i> (power) is the primary virtue. If one desires a game where it isn't, then that is up to those playing. But don't imagine that reality is the same. It never has been and it never will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, walk the talk. I would love to see examples from mythology backing your point. While you're at it, consider the following:<br /> <br /> Skanda, war general of the Devas is tricked out of the fruit of knowledge by his brother, the beloved Ganesha.<br /> <br /> The Apsara Tilottama is able to trick the Asura brothers Sunda and Upasunda, into killing each other.<br /> <br /> Huang Di, the Yellow Emperor, is threatened by the much larger army of Chi You. He evens the odds by convincing the rulers of the neighbouring nations to ally with him. So politically savvy is he, that at the end of thte war, all of them voluntarily join his kingdom.<br /> <br /> Bres the beautiful ruled the warriors of the Tuatha who could not lift a finger against him because he used his Charisma to convince them he would be the perfect candidate for king. Only Cairbre, the poet, is able to go against the king by writing Ireland's first satire. And it is glorious Nuada who finally drives him out.<br /> <br /> The great Scion Cu Chullain is tricked into his death by the manipulations of a hag (either the Morrigan or Mebd in disguise). The Morrigan had already weakened him before by tricking him into healing her, an act he had promised he would never do.<br /> <br /> The Orisha of Love, Oshun, is the only one who can trick Ogun, God of Iron into leaving his self-imposed exile. She alone can mesmerise the God of Death and steal his talismans of power.<br /> <br /> The juggernaut Set is ultimately defeated by the trickery of Isis and Horus.<br /> <br /> And Anansi, the tiny spider, earns his place amongst the Gods by outwitting such people as Python and Leopard.<br /> <br /> Even the mortal world is ruled by socials. For every thug on the street, a untouchable mob boss rules from the shadows. For every hard working citizen, a lobbyist gets his way. For every army led coup, a beloved general is ascendant. Imagine how much greater the Socials of Gods are.<br /> <br /> You're right: Our world is ruled by power, but that power has never been limited to those with the strongest arm. If you want more proof of that, just ask Tiger what happened to his balls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-08-2014, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:26:40-08:00","id":86968,"title":"","content":"(And yes, before someone starts screaming, I am aware that Neil Gaiman in all probability made that myth up in American Gods).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T15:04:36-08:00","id":87029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86902#post86902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole social vs physical argument has gotten me thinking: how do epic socials work on people without the appropriate method of perception. I'm thinking things along the lines of Odysseus' men plugging their ears to row past the (presumably possessed of epic socials) Sirens. It also means that in-the-know adversaries could easily get deaf security people in order to mitigate the damage that epic social characters can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely some powers that require your target to understand the language you are speaking, so that they can follow your commands to the letter. However, epic socials are generally going to transcend the need for many senses. This is especially true if you have epic perception of your own (and if you do not, that is a whole different set of problems).<br /> <br /> Even if you cannot hear, you can still see their body language, feel the vibrations of their words against your skin, and taste their emotional state in the air. Even if you cannot see, you can still smell the chemical changes in their body, and hear the whisper of the wind whenever they move their body. If you have multiple permanent handicaps at once then your storyteller may give you some bonuses to resisting those powers, in exchange for all the penalties you are going to be suffering in your daily adventuring. Otherwise whatever happened probably counts as a stunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Basically, when Odysseus' men plugged their ears to row past the Sirens, they were performing a stunt against a difficulty appropriate to their prowess.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:16:04-08:00","id":87067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87029#post87029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are definitely some powers that require your target to understand the language you are speaking, so that they can follow your commands to the letter. However, epic socials are generally going to transcend the need for many senses. This is especially true if you have epic perception of your own (and if you do not, that is a whole different set of problems).<br /> <br /> Even if you cannot hear, you can still see their body language, feel the vibrations of their words against your skin, and taste their emotional state in the air. Even if you cannot see, you can still smell the chemical changes in their body, and hear the whisper of the wind whenever they move their body. If you have multiple permanent handicaps at once then your storyteller may give you some bonuses to resisting those powers, in exchange for all the penalties you are going to be suffering in your daily adventuring. Otherwise whatever happened probably counts as a stunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Basically, when Odysseus' men plugged their ears to row past the Sirens, they were performing a stunt against a difficulty appropriate to their prowess.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes quite a lot of sense. I guess what I was thinking about would be a kind of social equivalent to Solipsistic Well-Being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:02:24-08:00","id":87115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87067#post87067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes quite a lot of sense. I guess what I was thinking about would be a kind of social equivalent to Solipsistic Well-Being.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much for what the Willpower-based resistance against mental manipulation is. Though, it's pretty much relegated to PC's and big bads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T19:58:34-08:00","id":87170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86966#post86966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heimdall is at war, under the commands of his Jarl, Odin. This is not a matter of Heimdall's resistance vs. Loki's Manipulation, it's a matter of Odin's Manipulation vs. Loki's Manipulation, and Odin wins out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Game versus Literature. Game work well for you. Lit..not so much.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86966#post86966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the mortal world is ruled by socials. For every thug on the street, a untouchable mob boss rules from the shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...let's get real here. Threat and intimidation is what works for the mob. And everyone know that you cross them, retaliation happens. If you're weak, you get eaten alive, and your operation gets taken over.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86966#post86966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For every hard working citizen, a lobbyist gets his way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lobbyist = money = power. Until he eats a bullet in a back alley.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86966#post86966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For every army led coup, a beloved general is ascendant. Imagine how much greater the Socials of Gods are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because ruthlessness is the name of the game. . A &quot;beloved&quot; general? Isn't that why tyrants wear such uniforms? Funny how the one thing a lot of nations wants are nukes. The most powerful nations are so armed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86966#post86966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right: Our world is ruled by power, but that power has never been limited to those with the strongest arm. If you want more proof of that, just ask Tiger what happened to his balls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask President Putin how that works.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=86944#post86944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, back this claim up with examples, at lest more than Samudra provided.<br /> Oh, and while you're at it. Only choose examples from mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! Really? How many does most pantheons make?<br /> Just maybe...you don't know that in almost every single pantheon in every culture since Mesopotamia there is a &quot;Leader-deity&quot; usually a king. S/He leads not because s/he's the smartest, but because s/he has the most power. Literature shows that some have that power stripped from them, but it has always been temporary because the &quot;order&quot; mandated from the gods needs to be enforced. This should have been obvious, painfully so. Perhaps I'm conflating reality with the game...but I'm a little wowed here. Zeus, Odin, Tezcatlipoca, Amaterasu, Marduk, Amun-Ra (and Re-Horakhty..among others. Ra has merged with several dieties), Shangdi etc......not the most clever of deities. They however have the most power. Sure, knock them down, but they are never down for the count. They've always returned to the top position.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:25:35-08:00","id":87211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87170#post87170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow! Really? How many does most pantheons make?<br /> Just maybe...you don't know that in almost every single pantheon in every culture since Mesopotamia there is a &quot;Leader-deity&quot; usually a king. S/He leads not because s/he's the smartest, but because s/he has the most power. Literature shows that some have that power stripped from them, but it has always been temporary because the &quot;order&quot; mandated from the gods needs to be enforced. This should have been obvious, painfully so. Perhaps I'm conflating reality with the game...but I'm a little wowed here. Zeus, Odin, Tezcatlipoca, Amaterasu, Marduk, Amun-Ra (and Re-Horakhty..among others. Ra has merged with several dieties), Shangdi etc......not the most clever of deities. They however have the most power. Sure, knock them down, but they are never down for the count. They've always returned to the top position.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking Socials versus Physicals, not Mentals versus Physicals. None of these deities is the smartest in the Pantheon (except for Odin) but they are amongst the most charismatic, manipulative and beautiful.<br /> <br /> Zeus! Since when is Zeus a physical badass? The ONE time he engages in physical combat, against Typhon, he literally gets ripped apart! Zeus rules through his Charisma, his thunderbolts and his authority as lawmaker of Olympus.<br /> <br /> Odin...really, Odin is ruler by dint of his physical stats? The same Odin who is insulted by Loki for never actually entering battle and staying behind casting spells? Odin rules by dint of the simple fact that it is impossible to argue with him, or to get the better of him. The only people who do, are Frigg and Loki, both Manipulation powerhouses themselves.<br /> <br /> Tezcatlipoca...Are we speaking of the same Tezcatlipoca who caused the end of the Fourth World by literally doing nothing but talking?<br /> <br /> Amaterasu...the same Amaterasu whose absence sent the other Gods into despair? The same Amaterasu who could only be brought out of the rock cave by another social character, Uzume? The same Amaterasu who deemed her beauty too great to keep away from the World? Who is literally so beautiful she bedazzles herself?<br /> <br /> Marduk...the same Marduk who defeated Tiamat by never even touching her but literally blowing her apart with wind? The same Marduk who had the sense to first finalize a social contract with the other Gods to make him king before running off to kill her?<br /> <br /> Ra? The same Ra who is a doddering old fool? Who cannot survive a snakebite? Who still commands the respect of a barge full of warriors? Who is ultimately defeated not by force of arms, but by the trickery of Isis?<br /> <br /> Shangdi...Shangdi, the transcendental one? Who most of the time does not even have a physical form, forget being a physical badass! Who is replaced by the even more corporeally uninterested Jade Emperor, who explicitly rules by force of enlightenment?<br /> <br /> Let me look at a few more...<br /> <br /> Indra, for all his physical might, is only King by the auspices of the Trimurti, who are equal parts Physical, Mental and Social.<br /> <br /> Mithra, for all his prowess as a warrior, is still only second-in-command to Ahura Mazda.<br /> <br /> Svarozhich, lord of the Slavic Gods, rules by simple fact of having created most of them. Of the Four Kings who rule under his authority, only Perun is physically capable. The others (Dazhbog, Radegast and Svantovit) are all Social and Mental characters first, Physical second. And Perun is regularly tricked by the trickster Veles.<br /> <br /> Nuada, High King of the Tuatha, is not the greatest of their warriors. The Dagda, Ogma, are all better by far. But it is his sheer force of Charisma that allows him to rule as beloved monarch and helps him regain the throne after he lost it.<br /> <br /> Shango might call himself King of the Orisha, but even he acknowledges the superiority of Eshu and Orunmila, Trickster God and Lord of Prophecy. He respects the wisdom of the latter, and is scared shitless of the antics of the latter, as is everyone else with the tiniest bit of sense in their heads.<br /> <br /> No Godking rules by dint of physical might alone. They rule because their subjects adore them enough to rule, and because they hold power over important aspects of the Universe. Zeus is king because of his Charisma and Thunder. Odin is jarl because of his Manipulation and Magic. Amaterasu is empress because of her Appearance and Sun. Not because of whatever Physical Attributes they might possess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T21:58:57-08:00","id":87227,"title":"","content":"The score is currently 27 to 0 in Samudra's favor. Shadowflame, I politely request that you start citing specific examples or honorably admit that you may have been wrong about your position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:04:17-08:00","id":87299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87170#post87170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game versus Literature. Game work well for you. Lit..not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you trying to tell me that Heimdall is not, in fact, fighting in the Ragnarok war under the command of Odin? Not to mention, you yourself commented that Loki's killing of Heimdall only happens because Fate ordained it. Have you considered that perhaps Fate also ordained that Heimdall would not fall for any of Loki's lies this time?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87170#post87170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...let's get real here. Threat and intimidation is what works for the mob. And everyone know that you cross them, retaliation happens. If you're weak, you get eaten alive, and your operation gets taken over.</div> </div> </div> </div>And 'Threat and Intimidation' are not social actions? Fear is an excellent avenue of social power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87170#post87170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lobbyist = money = power. Until he eats a bullet in a back alley.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lobbyists are not killed by random thugs, no more than any other individual. If specific measures are taken to eliminate them, such is done on the orders of other social characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87170#post87170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because ruthlessness is the name of the game. . A &quot;beloved&quot; general? Isn't that why tyrants wear such uniforms? Funny how the one thing a lot of nations wants are nukes. The most powerful nations are so armed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beloved by his army, which is why they put him on the throne. Feared by his people. As I noted above, fear is an equally valid avenue of social power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=87170#post87170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask President Putin how that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, India must not get the news channel that reported how Putin defeated his opponents in an arm-wrestling match.<br /> <br /> Whatever power Putin has, whatever forces he can command, whatever weapons he can bring to bear, he has achieved through social stats, through his position as President of a country that gives him those powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:53:25-07:00","id":88250,"title":"","content":"Hell, (last I counted) eight of Heracles' labors involved his having to think his way through the challenge rather than smash through it, and three of them required him <i>talking</i> his way past the &quot;true&quot; challenge. <b>Only</b> three of the challenges (the nemean lion, stymphalian birds, and cretan bull) were straightforward physical challenges (and in the case of the birds, Heracles was screwed but for Athena's intervention).<br /> <br /> Specifically in terms of social challenges, Heracles had to convince Artemis to spare her wrath for stealing her hind (which was Eurystheus' intent), had to convince Chiron to tell him how to capture the Erymanthian boar, <i>had </i>talked Hippolyta into simply giving Heracles her belt (until Hera decided to be Hera), had to convince Atlas to retrieve the Hesperides' apples for him (and then tricked him into taking back the World), and had to talk Hades into letting him capture Cerberus (and again, that Hades would never allow it was Eurystheus' plan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:36:06-07:00","id":88394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]The score is currently 27 to 0 in Samudra's favor. Shadowflame, I politely request that you start citing specific examples or honorably admit that you may have been wrong about your position.</div> </div> </div> </div> When it comes to reinterpretation, I can't argue with it. It's like someone debating the Bible and choosing to read it five different ways. How can anyone argue with that? If you want to believe in your interpretation...well... All I know is reality. If a fast talker walks into an alley full of gangbangers looking to put a hurt on him, he's not walking out. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Whatever power Putin has, whatever forces he can command, whatever weapons he can bring to bear, he has achieved through social stats, through his position as President of a country that gives him those powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> If this comforts you better than admitting the sheer power at his command (the blitz he did at Georgia...no other country wants to see again), then embrace it. A Third World country has no power, economically, nor militarily...no matter how they complain at the UN. The Sudan is a good example of a country that did whatever and there whole ethnic cleansing thing in Darfur that no one paid any attention to for a good year...and then still no one did anything. (UN is pretty much a paper tiger) Russia will do whatever it will, and the EU will look the other way as it costs them the Crimea. If Putting didn't have one of the most formidable militaries in the world...and the Ukraine did, he could talk, talk, talk, he still wouldn't get anything. Because it's always about power and the ability to kill) It's so easy to believe in social graces when you've army at your back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T14:21:21-07:00","id":88411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88394#post88394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When it comes to reinterpretation, I can't argue with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no reinterpretation going on here, only your misinterpretation of the characters of figures like Zeus, Odin and Ra. If you actually have, as you claim to have, more examples from myth of Physical overpowering Social than I have provided of the opposite, kindly provide them, or declare this discussion over.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, you may wish to peruse <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.in/2012/05/thunder-and-lightning.html\" target=\"_blank\">this post</a>; Anne explains the situation with Zeus far more eloquently than I could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88394#post88394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If this comforts you better than admitting the sheer power at his command...</div> </div> </div> </div>In what universe, pray tell, am I denying the might at his command? I am simply pointing out that it is might <b><i>at his command</i></b>, not <b><i>his might</i></b>. The Physical might of his army is unquestionable. It just so happens that the leash to that might is held by Putin by dint of his Social calibre, not his Physical calibre. He did not earn the right to command the army through participation in track and field events. He holds that power because he had the political savvy to work himself to the top, to a position that gives him an army to play around with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T14:27:03-07:00","id":88415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88394#post88394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...If this comforts you better than admitting the sheer power at his command (the blitz he did at Georgia...no other country wants to see again), then embrace it. A Third World country has no power, economically, nor militarily...no matter how they complain at the UN. The Sudan is a good example of a country that did whatever and there whole ethnic cleansing thing in Darfur that no one paid any attention to for a good year...and then still no one did anything. (UN is pretty much a paper tiger) Russia will do whatever it will, and the EU will look the other way as it costs them the Crimea. If Putting didn't have one of the most formidable militaries in the world...and the Ukraine did, he could talk, talk, talk, he still wouldn't get anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanna play the IR home game, let's play the IR home game.<br /> <br /> Of course, were this true Russia would have invaded Georgia and/or Ukraine at any time they desired to simply annex Abkhazia, South Ossetia, and Crimea. You can <i>definitely</i> add Kazakhstan, Uzbekistan, Belarus, and eastern Ukraine to the list, and <i>probably</i> eastern Poland, the rest of Ukraine, and several Baltic and Balkan states to the list as well. Yet, so far only Abkhazia, South Ossetia, and Crimea are under Russian occupation -- and for a very specific reason cited directly by Russia as <i>jus ad bellum</i>, the protection of ethnic Russians abroad.<br /> <br /> Now, why is that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it's always about power and the ability to kill) It's so easy to believe in social graces when you've army at your back. </div> </div> </div>Hint: this ain't it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T18:00:00-07:00","id":88532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88394#post88394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If this comforts you better than admitting the sheer power at his command (the blitz he did at Georgia...no other country wants to see again), then embrace it. A Third World country has no power, economically, nor militarily...no matter how they complain at the UN. The Sudan is a good example of a country that did whatever and there whole ethnic cleansing thing in Darfur that no one paid any attention to for a good year...and then still no one did anything. (UN is pretty much a paper tiger) Russia will do whatever it will, and the EU will look the other way as it costs them the Crimea. If Putting didn't have one of the most formidable militaries in the world...and the Ukraine did, he could talk, talk, talk, he still wouldn't get anything. Because it's always about power and the ability to kill) It's so easy to believe in social graces when you've army at your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be under the impression that military might and physical might are the same thing. They're not. If we were defining Putin's actions in game terms, it would not be Epic Strength, but rather use of the War Purview. You'll note that the Epic Strength and War are not always found in the same gods. Some, like Ares or Huitzilopochtli, are absolute murder machines who wade into combat themselves and start wrecking heads alongside their troops, but then you have strategists like Athena or Odin who are all about going to war and can even put up a good fight if they want to, but are much more regarded for their strategies or cleverness to bring about their victories. Hell, even many of the wrecking balls have socials to back them up. Huitzilopochtli, for example has Charisma out the wazoo, when he commands you, you do what he says, even if what he says is extremely detrimental to you (as his followers found out when they listened to his advice and followed his orders to kill the daughter of the one king they had as an ally and wear her flayed skin in front of him). <br /> <br /> So, military might and physical might are two different things. And, yes, Putin is currently using his military might as a cudgel in the game of international politics. Just as Cronus used his military might and prowess to rule over his Golden Age. And we know how that ended. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying the above to comment on the current state of world affairs (or to belittle or undermine anything about those unfortunate enough to be directly dealing with them), just to point out that the example you're giving is actually undermining your point. As has EVERY example you have thus far provided. Using Putin as an example of physical power being more potent than social prowess is only valid if Putin himself is on the front lines, dodging bullets, taking artillery shells to the face, and ripping tanks apart with his bare hands. It is only through social means, inspiring loyalty or coercion, or intimidation, that you have an army at your back. Without socials, or in supernatural terms, the War Purview, it is difficult to raise that army and convince it to live and die for you. <br /> <br /> The other hypothetical you keep pulling out is the smooth talker who runs into a gang of thugs and gets shot. Well, that's not necessarily the last laugh. Social characters have a lot of contacts and people willing to go to the mattresses for them. The thugs get arrested in the absolute best case scenario. There are many other possibilities, up to and including Keyser Soze levels of vengeance where the thugs watch everyone they've ever loved slaughtered before they finally get killed. This happens. Baldr dies and the entire Aesir lose their shit to make sure the monster who did it pays, and they're not that concerned when it turns out they got the wrong guy first. <br /> <br /> And the best smooth talkers, the Scions and the like with Epic Charisma or Manipulation? They're able to a) tell the thugs this before they shoot and b) get them to believe it. Loki's famous for pulling this exact scenario with Thjazi.<br /> <br /> Power comes in many forms. It comes in physical strength. It comes in crafty minds. It comes in powerful Relics. It comes with power over the elements and over Fate itself. Social power manages to be one of the best, because if you have Social power, then if you lack power in another form, be it military might or a magic sword or the ability to bench press a mountain, then you are better able to convince someone who HAS that power to help you, whether through charm, guile, sex appeal, or intimidation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T06:15:15-07:00","id":88805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88415#post88415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, were this true Russia would have invaded Georgia and/or Ukraine at any time they desired to simply annex Abkhazia, South Ossetia, and Crimea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You imagine that annexation is necessary just to maintain control? It isn't. The conflict began when Georgia wanted membership with NATO. Russia said no. In five days South Ossetia and Abkhazia was recognized by Russia as independent states (in case you're confused, this means that their under Russia's control), Russian troops all over considered as &quot;peacekeepers.&quot; Georgia tried retaking the area in 2008. Results; <i>Georgia loses control over parts of Abkhazia (25%) and former South Ossetia AO (40%) it previously held. Around 20% of Georgia (including Abkhazia and South Ossetia) is no longer under government control.</i> The end <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_South_Ossetia_war#Equipment_losses_and_cost\" target=\"_blank\">result</a>; <i>&quot;Russia has largely destroyed Georgia's war-fighting capability&quot;.</i> *shrugs* In effect a tributary. Just like every nation bordering Russia it seems. (an acquaintance of mine lived in Belarus for a while. She said all Moscow has to do is make a fist) <br /> I'm a little surprised at just how much wishful thinking is in so many posts. Either that, or you guys are more purely focused on the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T06:35:46-07:00","id":88810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88805#post88805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little surprised at just how much wishful thinking is in so many posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truly, the amount of wishful thinking in some of the recent posts is <i>staggering</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T07:40:23-07:00","id":88836,"title":"","content":"<i>Despite having no official capacity to do so, I hereby declare this debate concluded. Verdict in favor of the prosecutor due to overwhelming citation, and a stunning lack of citation from the defendant. Court is adjourned.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T08:55:08-07:00","id":88865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88805#post88805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You imagine that annexation is necessary just to maintain control? It isn't. The conflict began when Georgia wanted membership with NATO. Russia said no. In five days South Ossetia and Abkhazia was recognized by Russia as independent states (in case you're confused, this means that their under Russia's control), Russian troops all over considered as &quot;peacekeepers.&quot; Georgia tried retaking the area in 2008. Results; <i>Georgia loses control over parts of Abkhazia (25%) and former South Ossetia AO (40%) it previously held. Around 20% of Georgia (including Abkhazia and South Ossetia) is no longer under government control.</i> The end <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_South_Ossetia_war#Equipment_losses_and_cost\" target=\"_blank\">result</a>; <i>&quot;Russia has largely destroyed Georgia's war-fighting capability&quot;.</i> *shrugs* In effect a tributary. Just like every nation bordering Russia it seems. (an acquaintance of mine lived in Belarus for a while. She said all Moscow has to do is make a fist)<br /> I'm a little surprised at just how much wishful thinking is in so many posts. Either that, or you guys are more purely focused on the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow...you have <b>no</b> idea whatsoever what on Earth I'm -- or you're, for that matter -- talking about, do you.<br /> <br /> Hint: it has to do with <i>why</i> Russia invaded Abkhazia, South Ossetia, and Ukraine <i>at that point</i> rather than just any old time they felt like, and how those invasions were/are <i>justified</i> to the international community. Think just war theory. If might truly made right as you claim, that wouldn't have mattered and Russia needn't wait -- or justify those invasions to the outside world -- yet they <i>did</i>. Why?<br /> <br /> Oh, and just so we're clear, you just admitted yourself Russia is using its military as a piece in a much greater geopolitical game -- Realpolitik is an innately <i>social</i> game. Case in point the South Ossetia war <i>itself</i>, wherein the Russian Federation baited Georgia into invading so that it could justify an occupation under the Putin Doctrine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-11-2014, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T09:27:27-07:00","id":88876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88805#post88805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either that, or you guys are more purely focused on the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes we are purely focused on the game. The game is what we're discussing. The only reason we're talking about Russia's military is that you brought it up as an example to prove a point about the game and about mythology. And failed to realize, repeatedly, that the example you've been giving proves you wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T09:48:52-07:00","id":88887,"title":"","content":"Well, I thought I was talking about how strength (and the willingness to use it) is the prime virtue anywhere. If there's a gun to the head, there isn't a lot of social gaming here since the gun wielder is willing to pull the trigger. But I'm sure anyone and everyone will positively gush how smart, charming, wise,..etc, ad nauseum, to keep that trigger from being pulled.<br /> No matter how anyone fantasizes if Russia wasn't as powerful as it was, it would have gone very differently. Indeed, they would have lost. They wouldn't have destroyed Georgia's military so completely...and Georgia would have joined NATO giving it more power. I recall an old Stratfor report that mentioned stability would have pretty much gone out the window however. (If I find it I'll post it, but I'm sure no one really cares...Not that anyone gave a damn about Georgia, or for that matter the Ukraine today.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88810#post88810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truly, the amount of wishful thinking in some of the recent posts is <i>staggering</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reality sees over 200 causalities. So it's understandable why you'd post differently.<br /> <br /> Oh look! As predicted in this very thread (and likely elsewhere by others) Russia to Crimea; <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2014/03/11/world/europe/ukraine-crisis/index.html?hpt=hp_t2\" target=\"_blank\">Welcome back. We've missed you!</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T16:10:22-07:00","id":89087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=88887#post88887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I thought I was talking about how strength (and the willingness to use it) is the prime virtue anywhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Might I suggest actually reading what Realpolitik is before commenting upon it, and...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Not that anyone gave a damn about Georgia, or for that matter the Ukraine today. </div> </div> </div>...<b>wow</b>. I could go on about oil politics and Russia in the Black Sea region and Caucusus <b>alone</b> for probably longer than posting here would allow, and nuke your argument from orbit, <i>let alone</i> the importance of both Ukraine and Georgia to eastern Europe and central Asia as agricultural exporters, <i>or</i> the importance of Crimea to Russia as its only warm-water port, fossil fuels hub, and gateway to the Mediterranean as well as strategic importance vis-a-vis Turkey (an <b>actual</b> NATO member).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Dunning-Kruger_effect\" target=\"_blank\">You are literally so ignorant on this topic you can't even figure out you're wrong</a>, <a href=\"http://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Fractal_wrongness\" target=\"_blank\">let alone the depth and completeness of your wrongness</a>. You can't even figure out my most basic of points, which is that Russia only invaded these regions when they did because they had justification, which allowed them to elude international reprisal -- which is indicative of Russia's own comparative economic and military <i>weakenss</i> which in itself is counter-argument to your claims. You are so deep in the weeds here that an attempt to actually explain this is an utter waste of my time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:11:22-07:00","id":89125,"title":"","content":"You know, this topic has gone so far off the rails that the rails are on a separate continent, but until now, we'd been actually talking about things related to Scion and mythology. And now we're turning far, far away from that. The topic of Russian politics is starting to engulf the thread and is no longer even connected to the discussion about social vs. physical power. Not to mention that the argument has essentially devolved into throwing eggs at a brick wall. <br /> <br /> So, let me instead address an older point that was made...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=85369#post85369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithra has just a valid claim on being in the Roman pantheon as he does in the Persian/Zoroastrian one. Guanyin would likely be accepted by both Japan and China. Just saying: membership in one pantheon doesn't necessarily preclude membership in another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am definitely in favor of this general idea. Gods crossing over into other pantheons is a frequent occurrence and having rules to govern this sort of thing would be nice. The thing is, while admittedly I don't know how or if Pantheon Specific Purviews will work in 2e, but I am firmly against the idea of being able to have two of them. COMPLETELY against it. It's game-breaking. What advantages might membership in two pantheons get you? Cause I can see disadvantages clearly (Two or more sets of divine people getting all up in your business and demanding stuff of you? Possibly contradictory stuff?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:32:46-07:00","id":89133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89125#post89125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, this topic has gone so far off the rails that the rails are on a separate continent [. . .] What advantages might membership in two pantheons get you? Cause I can see disadvantages clearly (Two or more sets of divine people getting all up in your business and demanding stuff of you? Possibly contradictory stuff?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and honestly I feel this entire thing can be reconciled if TOP simply adds to the game rules for the same god in different aspects, or in differing pantheons. Take Ares, for example, who in Roman mythology as Mars was a deity of agriculture, guardianship and civic virtue. That way, one doesn't have to worry about being beholden to two different pantheons, or get other fun balance-related issues -- just swap virtues and associations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-11-2014, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:22:36-07:00","id":89154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89133#post89133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Take Ares, for example, who in Roman mythology as Mars was a deity of agriculture, guardianship and civic virtue. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, he's that too. He's still very much a god of war, of virility, of the legions. A boy becomes a man, meaning he can join the Legions, when he shaves his first beard and burns it in the temple of Mars. When a legionnaire can't get enough of army life and re-ups for another 20 years, becoming one of the evocati, he goes to the Temple of Mars to make the vow, drenched in the blood of his sacrifice. Mars is very much a god of war.<br /> <br /> He's just not a screaming bully one second away from a temper-tantrum like Ares. <br /> <br /> Maybe he just grew up? After getting his ass handed to him by a mortal during the Trojan War and getting insufficient sympathy, perhaps he had a moment.<br /> <br /> Oh wait. It's Scion. No way that a mortal non-Scion could ever ever ever ever defeat a god. Silly, silly Homer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T19:08:28-07:00","id":89171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89154#post89154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh wait. It's Scion. No way that a mortal non-Scion could ever ever ever ever defeat a god. Silly, silly Homer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well actually that's really not irreconcilable at all, seeing as Avatar available at God allows you to just lower your legend and be on par with mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T20:04:02-07:00","id":89195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89154#post89154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, he's that too. He's still very much a god of war, of virility, of the legions. A boy becomes a man, meaning he can join the Legions, when he shaves his first beard and burns it in the temple of Mars. When a legionnaire can't get enough of army life and re-ups for another 20 years, becoming one of the evocati, he goes to the Temple of Mars to make the vow, drenched in the blood of his sacrifice. Mars is very much a god of war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it was <i>after</i> Hellenization of the Republic that Mars came to represent war as well. Don't forget that military service was considered an expression and embodiment of <i>virtus</i><i>, </i>hence the special connection to Mars and the military.<br /> <br /> Jupiter was also a patron-deity of the legions as well, especially in the early Imperial period (the aquila is iconography of Jupiter). At least, until Mithraism started sneaking into the legions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh wait. It's Scion. No way that a mortal non-Scion could ever ever ever ever defeat a god. Silly, silly Homer. </div> </div> </div>Hubris, man. Ubiquitous in Greek literature, the unifying trait of the entire Dodekatheon, and especially lurved by Homer. Diomedes also had help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-11-2014, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T21:09:45-07:00","id":89232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are literally so ignorant on this topic you can't even figure out you're wrong, let alone the depth and completeness of your wrongness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I'm sure you feel better now. My links went unread because they didn't support any of your...beliefs. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't even figure out my most basic of points, which is that Russia only invaded these regions when they did because they had justification...</div> </div> </div> </div> ROFLMAO!!! Justification...? Was a fabrication in the same vein as US fabrication for the Iraq Debacle. One of Putin's very loud and clear messages in his press conference a few days ago was that if you guys can invade another country on a completely trumped-up pretext, so can I. And he won't pay a price. NATO won't lift a finger because as much as the EU talks about it, <a href=\"http://money.cnn.com/2014/03/04/news/economy/europe-russia-ukraine/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">they've too much invested</a>; <i>...With the eurozone still emerging from its own crisis, European leaders will think long and hard about any measures that might put that recovery at risk. Russia is the EU's third-biggest trading partner after the U.S. and China. Trade in goods totaled a record 336 billion euros ($462 billion) in 2012, more than 10 times the volume between Russia and the U.S. Add in exports of services, and the value of the Russia-EU relationship rises to $520 billion. <b>Russia is the EU's single-biggest supplier of energy</b>. Oil and gas prices rose sharply Monday on fear of supply disruptions through Ukraine, which account for about half of Russian flows. EU exports, meanwhile, are largely made up of machinery and transport, chemicals, medicines and agricultural products. Nowhere is Europe's reliance on Russian energy more acute than in Germany. Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder is chairman of the shareholders' committee of Nord Stream, a joint venture between Russian gas giant Gazprom (GZPFY) and four big energy companies -- two from Germany, and one each from the Netherlands and France. </i> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">which allowed them to elude international reprisal -- which is indicative of Russia's own comparative economic and military weakenss which in itself is counter-argument to your claims. You are so deep in the weeds here that an attempt to actually explain this is an utter waste of my time.</div> </div> </div> </div> You want to believe differently. I should have understood that sooner. My apologies for wasting time posting links that I should have realized you would never read. Such as the <a href=\"http://www.stratfor.com/weekly/russo_georgian_war_and_balance_power\" target=\"_blank\">Stratfor article</a> mentioned in my earlier post. Moving along...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T21:55:06-07:00","id":89255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xegek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89171#post89171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well actually that's really not irreconcilable at all, seeing as Avatar available at God allows you to just lower your legend and be on par with mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, the Greek Gods have Valour. It would probably force them to even the odds if they were ever competing against mortals. Helps explain the Athena-Arachne situation too.<br /> <br /> By the way, a question for those in this forum better versed in the subject than I am: I know that Mithra was widely worshipped amongst Roman legions, but was he ever worshipped as part of the Roman Pantheon? As far as I know, he was always worshipped as an independent deity.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd, to that end, should a God be considered part of a Pantheon just because he was worshipped by the same people? I can see Sarasvati as a Goddess legitimately belonging to two different Pantheons, because she is actually worshipped as both the Deva Sarasvati and the Kami Benzaitan. But Mithra was always a Persian God who just happened to be worshipped in Rome. With great devotion and fanfare, undoubtedly, but not as a member of the same group of Gods as Jupiter or Mars. Again, my knowledge on this is lacking (I'm far better versed in mythology than I am in religion), so any corrections are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T02:51:16-07:00","id":89365,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Please get this thread back on topic. This is not the place to discuss the Ukraine situation. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T07:09:40-07:00","id":89454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89255#post89255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, a question for those in this forum better versed in the subject than I am: I know that Mithra was widely worshipped amongst Roman legions, but was he ever worshipped as part of the Roman Pantheon? As far as I know, he was always worshipped as an independent deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to keep in mind were the Romans were the God-Borg. They just kind of assimilated religious beliefs and cults, a lot like Christianity does today. Not being &quot;in the pantheon&quot; itself is something of a misnomer, since nearly every time you read about a Roman pantheon it's limited strictly to romanized classical Greek deities, rather than even hellenized classical Roman deities (so, the classification itself is rather arbitrary).<br /> <br /> This is mostly <b>if</b> I remember correctly -- it's been forever since I've studied my Roman history, and may be mistaken in places. The best place to start with Mithraism in the Roman Empire is sun worship. Sun worship predated Mithraism for a few centuries -- during the Republic period there was worship of <i>Sol indiges</i> which is believed to be a mishmash of various sun cults (and the Romans' own Phoebus) and Apollo during hellenization, and by the beginning of the Imperial period sun cults were completely dominated by romanized Apollo worship. During the Imperial period, there was a rebirth in sun worship (<i>Sol invictus</i>) through which Mithraism worked its way into Roman religion (interpreting Mithra as a solar deity with a bunch of other Roman virtues tacked on).<br /> <br /> If you <i>really</i> wanted to put it in Scion terms and play it straight, with that in mind Roman Mithraism would actually be a titan cult (Akhenaten). Would certainly make sense, considering Akhenaten's other pet projects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAnd, to that end, should a God be considered part of a Pantheon just because he was worshipped by the same people? I can see Sarasvati as a Goddess legitimately belonging to two different Pantheons, because she is actually worshipped as both the Deva Sarasvati and the Kami Benzaitan. But Mithra was always a Persian God who just happened to be worshipped in Rome. With great devotion and fanfare, undoubtedly, but not as a member of the same group of Gods as Jupiter or Mars. Again, my knowledge on this is lacking (I'm far better versed in mythology than I am in religion), so any corrections are welcome. </div> </div> </div>That's why I believe there should be rules for gods having different aspects, and being worshiped and producing scions of different aspects. Perhaps something like once a god hits Legend 12, their current Fatebonds, abilities, and purviews become &quot;locked in&quot; (they can continue improving associations up to their respective Ultimates, but no new stuff) -- and if they become further Fatebound, they develop multiple avatars to reflect the new Fatebonds rather than get new goodies to their original avatar.<br /> <br /> That way you get an alternate route for character progression at the god level while maintaining a semblance of game balance, and a venue for ancient gods having associations with multiple pantheons <i>while also</i> allowing classical deities taking on more modernized roles, but not threatening scions with obsolescence. Not to mention, it would provide an actual explanation as to why characters that have been around for dozens of millennia have such limited character sheets -- they had other avatars and associated Legends to build -- and provide for rebirth and regrowth of forgotten or &quot;dead&quot; gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-12-2014, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T09:32:25-07:00","id":89535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xegek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89171#post89171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well actually that's really not irreconcilable at all, seeing as Avatar available at God allows you to just lower your legend and be on par with mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... Yes... That works. Ares (and Aphrodite) were trying to get involved under Zeus' radar... It was before he said &quot;Hands off!&quot; but I'm sure that he was already fuming over the way the war was affecting morale. <br /> <br /> And it's a good illustration of the risks of using Avatar. They got HURT, by a MORTAL! (A Legendary Mortal at the very least with all the gods peppering Diomedes' family tree). <br /> <br /> I guess another point would be the &quot;you must be a grandchild&quot; rule to make the leap to Hero seems... artificially limiting. Achilles = Hero, Agamemnon &amp; Meneleus = Hero, Helen = Hero, but Diomedes, Ajax the Greater, Odysseus = NOT Hero.... I don't buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T09:35:40-07:00","id":89539,"title":"","content":"Mithra never joined up. Isis never joined up. Hell, Ba'al never joined up either. But they were all worshiped in Rome proper. They just weren't Graeco-Roman gods. And the Romans officially had BIG problems with them all. Proper Romans weren't supposed to go in for that nonsense. (The Ba'al thing got the Emperor in question offed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T09:55:48-07:00","id":89547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/81399-what-will-you-pantheons-be-like?p=89535#post89535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And it's a good illustration of the risks of using Avatar. They got HURT, by a MORTAL! (A Legendary Mortal at the very least with all the gods peppering Diomedes' family tree)...</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, in this particular case it doesn't even <i>have</i> to be drawn down to avatar. At that point, Hera had already told Zeus that Ares and Aphrodite were messing around, and Zeus sent Athena to deal with it (she'd already been helping Diomedes on the QT). Athena protected Diomedes from Ares, and guided his spear to strike the god. Frankly, at that point in the <i>Iliad</i> it was god versus god, and Diomedes was the poor bastard stuck in the thick of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}